AB  - To systematically grasp the path and trend of artificial intelligence empowering the operation risk management and control of power enterprises, this study has sorted out the cutting-edge literature in this field in the past five years and constructed a full-chain analysis framework for risk identification, assessment and prediction, and control and decision-making. Research has found that artificial intelligence technology demonstrates significant advantages in the six key elements of risk identification, assessment and prediction, as well as safety control, and can effectively enhance the intelligent level and efficiency of operational risk control in power enterprises. However, current applications still face challenges such as data security risks and the difficulty of cross-system collaboration. In the future, with the continuous integration of new technologies and the further improvement of their intelligence levels, the application of artificial intelligence technology in the operation risk control of power enterprises will become more extensive and in-depth.
